15
00:01:06,809 --> 00:01:11,056
A workflow is a file that tells
GitHub Actions which jobs to run.

16
00:01:11,096 --> 00:01:16,464
Here you look at it again for delivery:
what identifies an image, and how an image

17
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:18,443
is tied to exactly one commit.

18
00:01:18,783 --> 00:01:23,680
The second thread is release automation,
in outline, as the section gives it: three

19
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:28,676
facts and one trap. A release is a GitHub
record that points at a tag and adds notes

20
00:01:28,716 --> 00:01:33,613
and files. The trap is the reason a release
created by a workflow so often triggers

21
00:01:33,653 --> 00:01:34,089
nothing.

22
00:01:34,429 --> 00:01:39,064
The local demonstration is about the Git
side of identity: is the working tree

23
