154
00:11:09,768 --> 00:11:11,416
Five mistakes to watch for.

155
00:11:11,756 --> 00:11:17,181
Deploying by a tag such as latest or main.
Root cause: a tag is a movable name,

156
00:11:17,221 --> 00:11:21,332
exactly like a branch; only the
digest identifies the image.

157
00:11:21,672 --> 00:11:26,684
Building a release image on a laptop. Root
cause: the working tree may differ from

158
00:11:26,724 --> 00:11:30,195
the commit it claims to be; a
runner's checkout is clean.

159
00:11:30,535 --> 00:11:34,289
A release workflow that waits for
an event its own token caused.

160
00:11:34,329 --> 00:11:39,151
Root cause: events caused by the GITHUB_TOKEN
do not start new workflow runs, with

161
00:11:39,191 --> 00:11:40,218
narrow exceptions.

162
00:11:40,558 --> 00:11:44,704
Deriving the version from a tag in
a job with the default checkout.

163
00:11:44,744 --> 00:11:49,202
Root cause: one commit and no tags,
so git describe has nothing to find.

164
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:52,625
Omitting context: . after
steps that changed files.

165
00:11:52,665 --> 00:11:57,463
Root cause: by default the build action
builds from the Git context and ignores

166
00:11:57,503 --> 00:11:58,626
local file changes.

167
00:12:00,466 --> 00:12:04,990
Now, out of the lab. A team that serves
a ranking model has two workflows.

168
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:10,171
The first runs on pushes to main: it tests,
computes the next version, and creates a

169
00:12:10,211 --> 00:12:15,167
release with the job token. The second has
the trigger on: release and builds and

170
00:12:15,207 --> 00:12:18,312
publishes the image. The
first workflow goes green.

171
00:12:18,352 --> 00:12:23,493
A release appears. The second workflow never
starts, and for a day people look for a

172
00:12:23,533 --> 00:12:25,219
typing error in its trigger.

173
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:30,244
There is none. The release was created by
the GITHUB_TOKEN, and events caused by

174
00:12:30,284 --> 00:12:32,666
that token don't start new workflow runs.

175
00:12:33,006 --> 00:12:38,008
The team chooses the first of the textbook's
two repairs: one workflow, with the

176
00:12:38,048 --> 00:12:43,239
image job chained after the release job by
needs. In the same change, the image job

177
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:48,533
stops deploying latest. It writes the digest
and the commit ID into its job summary,

178
00:12:48,573 --> 00:12:53,639
and the deploy job refers to the image by
digest. The on-call engineer's question

179
00:12:53,679 --> 00:12:55,277
now has a one-line answer.

