197
00:14:18,098 --> 00:14:19,758
You should now be able to say:

198
00:14:20,098 --> 00:14:25,394
An image is identified by its digest; a
tag is a movable name, like a branch.

199
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:29,528
Deploy by digest and record the
digest and the commit ID together.

200
00:14:29,868 --> 00:14:35,953
git describe --tags --match names a commit
relative to the release tags, and --dirty

201
00:14:35,993 --> 00:14:38,724
says when the tree is not that commit.

202
00:14:39,064 --> 00:14:43,682
A tag-driven release job needs the tags and
the history, which the default checkout

203
00:14:43,722 --> 00:14:44,524
does not fetch.

204
00:14:44,864 --> 00:14:50,080
Events caused by the job token start no new
workflow runs: chain jobs with needs, or

205
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,519
